WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.834
New details

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:01.034
in the

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.902
investigation into those four Americans

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.871
kidnaped in Mexico last week.

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:05.705
Local officials say

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:07.474
one person has been detained

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:08.742
after two of the U.S.

00:00:08.742 --> 00:00:10.643
citizens were found dead

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:12.512
in the border town of Matamoros.

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:14.280
The two others are thankfully alive,

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.548
although one is severely injured,

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:16.950
according to a U.S. official.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:17.917
And those two have returned

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:18.718
to the United States

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:20.687
for medical treatment and observation.

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:21.388
Family members

00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:23.289
say that the four were a tight knit

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:24.891
group of friends traveling

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.659
from South Carolina to Mexico,

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:27.727
so that one of them

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:29.529
could get a medical procedure done

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:30.296
across the border.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:32.899
But once they crossed from Texas

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:34.801
into Matamoros.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:37.137
Friends believe that the group got lost

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:38.638
and was then abducted.

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:39.606
The Justice Department

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:40.907
White House and State Department

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:41.741
say they are working

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:42.742
with Mexican officials

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:44.411
to find those responsible

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:45.211
and also to figure out

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:46.780
exactly what went wrong.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:47.147
U.S.

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:48.415
official previously told CNN

00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:50.050
they believe a Mexican cartel

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.151
likely mistook

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:52.352
the four Americans

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:54.354
or Haitian drug smugglers.

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:55.622
Our reporters are covering

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:57.257
every angle of this story.

00:00:57.257 --> 00:00:58.892
CNN's Rosa Flores starts us off

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.060
from the border town

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.127
of Brownsville, Texas,

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.429
where officials have identified the

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:04.164
victims and the survivors.

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:07.500
Two of four missing Americans

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.802
are back in the United States.

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:10.904
And receiving medical treatment in Texas

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:13.039
after being kidnaped in Mexico.

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:13.940
After what a U.S.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.308
official tells CNN

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:17.610
was a case of mistaken identity.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.779
Two members of the party were found dead

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:21.047
and one of the survivors

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:22.182
is severely injured

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:23.950
with a bullet wound to his leg.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.218
According to U.S.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:26.920
and Mexican officials

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.721
in the party of four Latvia.

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:29.622
Washington McGee

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:31.257
and Erik Williams survived.

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:33.326
Zin del Brown and Shaheed

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:35.028
Woodward were killed.

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:36.029
They crossed the border

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:37.163
from Brownsville, Texas,

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:39.232
into Matamoros, Mexico on Friday

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:41.668
for McGee to obtain a medical procedure,

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.770
according to a friend of McGee's.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.371
They drove a white minivan

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:46.673
with North Carolina plates

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:47.607
across the border

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:48.308
and got lost

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:50.276
while trying to locate the medical clinic

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:51.344
where they were headed.

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:53.179
The friend told CNN

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:54.147
before they were able

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:55.381
to locate the clinic.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:57.450
Disturbing video shows the aftermath

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:58.451
of the kidnaping

00:01:58.451 --> 00:01:59.953
as heavily armed men

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:02.055
loaded them into a white truck

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:03.089
and transported them

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:05.191
to various locations to evade capture.

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:06.860
According to Mexican officials,

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:09.496
travel got a lot of responsibilities.

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:11.464
The Mexican president saying today

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:12.732
during a news conference

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:13.900
that those responsible

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.969
will be found and punished. A U.S.

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:16.803
official familiar

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:17.971
with the investigation

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:20.607
told CNN they believe a Mexican cartel

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:21.774
kidnaped the group

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.643
after mistaking them for Haitian

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:24.577
drug smugglers.

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:25.645
Mexico's president

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:26.613
saying the Americans

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:28.014
were caught in a confrontation

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:29.616
between two groups.

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:30.483
The State Department

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:31.651
has issued its highest

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:33.353
level four warning

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:35.522
do not travel to Tamaulipas state

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:37.290
where the group was abducted

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.358
due to heavy crime

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:39.926
and kidnaping in the region.

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:40.860
There are many people

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.428
who cross over that border

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:44.397
for these medical appointments.

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:45.198
Attacks on U.S.

00:02:45.198 --> 00:02:47.066
citizens are unacceptable.

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:48.801
No matter where or under

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.970
what circumstances they occur.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:53.072
McGee and Williams are now under the care

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:54.574
of the FBI, and U.S.

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:55.308
officials

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:56.376
are making arrangements

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:57.010
to bring home

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:59.679
the bodies of Brown and Woodard.

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:00.780
Our immediate concerns

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.415
are for the safe return of our citizens

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:07.320
The building that you

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:07.921
see behind me

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:09.222
is a hospital where we believe

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:10.456
that the American survivors

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:11.191
are being treated.

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:13.059
The hospital is not issuing a statement

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:14.460
or reporting their conditions.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.563
But we do know from Mexican officials

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:17.497
that they are releasing

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:20.200
a timeline of this search.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.334
They say that they are even

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:22.769
releasing photographs

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:23.770
of some of the vehicles

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.138
that were used by kidnapers

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:26.873
and that at least one individual,

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:27.840
a 24 year old

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.842
who was doing some surveillance on

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:32.312
the Americans has been arrested.

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:32.612
And, Jake,

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.414
it's important to note that the Mexicans

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:36.149
and Mexican officials say

00:03:36.149 --> 00:03:38.351
that the American law enforcement

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:40.653
was not involved during this search Jake.

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:41.087
All right.

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:41.788
Rosa Flores,

00:03:41.788 --> 00:03:43.590
thank you so much, in Brownsville. Texas.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:44.557
Let's bring in

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:46.159
CNN security reporter Josh Campbell.

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:46.526
And Josh,

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:47.493
the Justice Department

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:48.628
says that it is working

00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:49.896
closely with the State Department

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:50.597
on this case.

00:03:50.597 --> 00:03:53.366
What is the role of a

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:56.202
investigation into this matter in Mexico?

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:57.170
Well,

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:58.738
this is an entire whole of government

00:03:58.738 --> 00:03:59.739
approach is how U.S.

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:00.974
officials are describing this.

00:04:00.974 --> 00:04:02.141
So in the United States

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:03.443
embassy, you have the ambassador

00:04:03.443 --> 00:04:04.210
but also in

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:05.612
what's called the country team,

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:07.580
a host of various different agencies

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:08.281
that convene

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:09.482
and what's called an emergency

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:10.183
action committee

00:04:10.183 --> 00:04:12.318
when you have a major incident like this.

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:13.419
All of those agencies

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:15.355
bring to bear certain things like that.

00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:16.289
The Drug Enforcement

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:17.156
Administration, obviously,

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:18.091
the State Department

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:19.726
working the diplomatic angle.

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:20.994
And then, of course, the FBI,

00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:21.427
which, you know,

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:22.762
has been involved from the beginning

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:24.597
to leverage their intelligence,

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:25.565
their human informant,

00:04:25.565 --> 00:04:26.833
signals intelligence,

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:28.868
working with their close partners

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:29.802
there in Mexico.

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:30.970
I'm told there are very close

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:33.239
relationships between FBI agents

00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:34.374
and Mexican authorities.

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:35.908
And so all of that was being leveraged

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:37.577
in order to try to identify

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:38.811
where these victims are.

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:39.879
It's also worth pointing out that

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:41.781
although we are now getting a resolution,

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:43.216
a very tragic resolution,

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:44.217
here to this incident,

00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:45.318
the investigation is not over.

00:04:45.318 --> 00:04:45.918
The FBI

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:47.787
still offering a $50,000 reward

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:49.022
leading to the identification

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:50.657
and prosecution of these captors.

00:04:50.657 --> 00:04:51.257
Ultimately,

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:53.059
do you think the U.S., assuming

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:54.460
that any suspects are captured,

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.261
do you think the U.S.

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:56.029
will request

00:04:56.029 --> 00:04:57.797
extradition, given that the crimes

00:04:57.797 --> 00:04:59.832
were committed against Americans?

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:01.200
I suspect the request will be made.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:01.934
It's yet to be seen

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.269
whether Mexican officials

00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:04.270
will adhere to that.

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:05.338
Now, on his face,

00:05:05.338 --> 00:05:06.606
this appears to be an incident

00:05:06.606 --> 00:05:07.774
that would fall under the U.S.

00:05:07.774 --> 00:05:08.608
Mexico treaty,

00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:09.275
where you have

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:11.010
the attack on Americans,

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.879
the killing, the murder of Americans

00:05:12.879 --> 00:05:15.148
and so that could fall under the treaty.

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:16.149
But it's worth pointing out,

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:16.616
our colleague

00:05:16.616 --> 00:05:17.383
Gustavo Valdes,

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:18.351
has been pointing this out

00:05:18.351 --> 00:05:19.752
so important that it wasn't

00:05:19.752 --> 00:05:20.620
just Americans

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:21.888
who were killed in this attack.

00:05:21.888 --> 00:05:22.288
Of course,

00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:23.556
there was a 22 year

00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:24.157
old girl,

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:25.358
a Mexican national,

00:05:25.358 --> 00:05:26.993
on her way to pick up her child,

00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:28.094
who was also caught

00:05:28.094 --> 00:05:30.129
in the crossfire of this cartel group

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:31.397
that my source tells me

00:05:31.397 --> 00:05:32.465
they thought they were attacking

00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:33.333
Haitian nationals.

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:33.900
They end up

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.702
killing these two Americans,

00:05:35.702 --> 00:05:36.869
injuring the others,

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:38.171
and then killing this 22 year

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:39.005
old Mexican national.

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:40.473
So I think to your question, Jake,

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:41.307
Mexican officials

00:05:41.307 --> 00:05:42.408
could also make a case and look,

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:43.876
we will prosecute this here

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:44.777
in our country,

00:05:44.777 --> 00:05:47.013
still ensuring that justice is served.

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:47.313
But again,

00:05:47.313 --> 00:05:48.114
I think the discussion

00:05:48.114 --> 00:05:49.315
about how that will be done

00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:49.916
will come later.

00:05:49.916 --> 00:05:50.183
First,

00:05:50.183 --> 00:05:52.352
the focus now is finding the suspects.

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:53.419
All right, Josh Campbell, thanks.

00:05:53.419 --> 00:05:54.721
Mexico is the second

00:05:54.721 --> 00:05:56.222
most popular destination

00:05:56.222 --> 00:05:58.858
for medical tourism globally,

00:05:58.891 --> 00:06:00.326
according to Patients Without Borders.

00:06:00.326 --> 00:06:01.327
That's an international health

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:02.829
care consulting company.

00:06:02.829 --> 00:06:03.763
That group estimates up

00:06:03.763 --> 00:06:04.697
to 3 million

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:05.398
people travel

00:06:05.398 --> 00:06:07.200
to Mexico every year to take advantage

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.501
of inexpensive treatments.

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:10.937
Americans can save between 40 and 60%

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:13.072
on common medical procedures.

00:06:13.072 --> 00:06:14.707
But of course, they're also taking risks

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:16.109
because these clinics

00:06:16.109 --> 00:06:18.211
are not held to U.S. standards.

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:20.947
CNN Espanol correspondent Gustavo

00:06:21.114 --> 00:06:22.682
Gustavo Valdes joins me now.

00:06:22.682 --> 00:06:23.316
Gustavo,

00:06:23.316 --> 00:06:24.951
you've been to some of these towns

00:06:24.951 --> 00:06:25.551
that are designed

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:27.153
to draw Americans across the border

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:29.188
specifically for medical care.

00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:31.591
Tell us about that. Hey, Jake.

00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:33.393
Every time you cross into Mexico,

00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:34.293
the very first thing

00:06:34.293 --> 00:06:35.595
you're more likely to see

00:06:35.595 --> 00:06:37.830
is either a pharmacy or a clinic

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:39.465
offering some kind of service

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:40.166
to Americans

00:06:40.166 --> 00:06:41.768
who are looking for a cheaper option

00:06:41.768 --> 00:06:43.136
to pay for health care.

00:06:43.136 --> 00:06:44.937
South of the border, typically

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:46.873
in this part of the country, in Mexico

00:06:46.873 --> 00:06:47.840
and Tamaulipas,

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:50.243
you will find dentist services

00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:51.511
that is the most common.

00:06:51.511 --> 00:06:56.516
The cosmetic surgery, the weight control

00:06:56.749 --> 00:06:57.383
procedures

00:06:57.383 --> 00:06:59.552
are typically done in larger cities

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:01.087
where they have larger hospitals

00:07:01.087 --> 00:07:03.523
because they require more

00:07:03.523 --> 00:07:05.091
care after the treatment.

00:07:05.091 --> 00:07:07.026
But there is one town in particular

00:07:07.026 --> 00:07:07.894
in this area

00:07:07.894 --> 00:07:09.929
and the Tamaulipas border is controlled.

00:07:09.929 --> 00:07:10.730
Progresso

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:13.232
where you see rows and rows of buildings.

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:14.333
They could be pharmacies,

00:07:14.333 --> 00:07:17.303
they could be stores selling drugs.

00:07:17.303 --> 00:07:19.071
They also have clinics

00:07:19.071 --> 00:07:20.506
that are offering the services

00:07:20.506 --> 00:07:20.973
and right now,

00:07:20.973 --> 00:07:22.742
they're very popular with Americans

00:07:22.742 --> 00:07:23.976
who spend the winter

00:07:23.976 --> 00:07:25.878
south in warmer climates.

00:07:25.878 --> 00:07:27.947
And now they're going back to their homes

00:07:27.947 --> 00:07:29.081
with Mexican drug.

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:30.850
There are cheaper And Gustavo,

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:31.851
what more can you tell us

00:07:31.851 --> 00:07:33.553
about the town of Matamoros

00:07:33.553 --> 00:07:35.154
and the surrounding areas?

00:07:35.154 --> 00:07:36.656
Are they dangerous?

00:07:36.656 --> 00:07:39.025
They are for the most part.

00:07:39.025 --> 00:07:39.725
They are taxed

00:07:39.725 --> 00:07:41.761
like the one we saw are reserved

00:07:42.028 --> 00:07:44.864
for confrontations among the cartel,

00:07:44.864 --> 00:07:45.698
some cartel members.

00:07:45.698 --> 00:07:46.532
This is a state

00:07:46.532 --> 00:07:47.900
that is home to the cartel

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:49.268
del gold for the Gulf cartel.

00:07:49.268 --> 00:07:51.237
So it is a very violent

00:07:51.237 --> 00:07:52.638
criminal organization.

00:07:52.638 --> 00:07:53.606
But typically

00:07:53.606 --> 00:07:54.607
you see these

00:07:54.607 --> 00:07:56.342
attacks among themselves

00:07:56.342 --> 00:07:58.611
and what you see is collateral damage

00:07:58.611 --> 00:07:59.712
like we saw with this woman

00:07:59.712 --> 00:08:01.814
who was shot in this confrontation

00:08:01.981 --> 00:08:03.716
with the four Americans.

00:08:03.716 --> 00:08:04.116
Typically,

00:08:04.116 --> 00:08:05.551
Americans are safe

00:08:05.551 --> 00:08:07.653
as long as they are there during the day.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:08.588
Typically

00:08:08.588 --> 00:08:10.189
the criminal organizations

00:08:10.189 --> 00:08:11.090
that want to get into

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:12.525
this kind of publicity.

00:08:12.525 --> 00:08:14.627
But the danger is always there.

00:08:15.094 --> 00:08:16.262
That's why it is.

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:18.498
There is a State Department

00:08:18.498 --> 00:08:20.533
has the alert to be careful

00:08:20.533 --> 00:08:21.868
when you cross into Mexico,

00:08:21.868 --> 00:08:24.003
especially in this part of the country.

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:24.437
All right.

00:08:24.437 --> 00:08:25.104
CNN's

00:08:25.371 --> 00:08:26.539
Honors by New York

00:08:26.539 --> 00:08:27.740
correspondent Gustavo about this.

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:28.674
Thank you so much. Appreciate it.

